# Reflaxe.Elixir Build Configuration
# Generated by mix haxe.gen.project
#
# Notes
# - `-lib reflaxe.elixir` initializes the compiler (via haxe_libraries/reflaxe.elixir.hxml).
# - Add the modules you want to compile at the bottom (one per line).

# Libraries
-lib reflaxe.elixir

# Source directories
-cp src_haxe

# Output directory for generated .ex files
-D elixir_output=lib

# Target selection is supplied by `-lib reflaxe.elixir`.

# Elixir is not a UTF-16 platform
-D no-utf16

# Application module prefix
#
# IMPORTANT:
# In Phoenix projects, this should match the app's Elixir module prefix (e.g. PhoenixChat)
# so framework transforms (Presence/Endpoint/Router/etc.) derive correct otp_app and PubSub modules.
-D app_name=PhoenixChat

# Optional canonical Mix formatting after code generation (off by default)
# -D reflaxe_elixir_format=write

# Enable dead code elimination to remove unused functions and reduce output noise
-dce full

# Convert HXX render strings to `~H` sigils (recommended for LiveView)
-D hxx_string_to_sigil

PhoenixChat
PhoenixChatRouter
phoenix_chat_hx.live.AppLive
phoenix_chat_hx.presence.ChatPresence
phoenix_chat_hx.Main
phoenix_chat_hx.utils.StringUtils
phoenix_chat_hx.utils.MathHelper
